GradeTrackr – Changelog

---

[v1.0] – 2025-08-15
Added
- Created initial 2D array for storing student test scores
- Included sample dataset with students and 3 subjects (Math, Science, English)
- Set up basic project structure

---

[v1.1] – 2025-08-29
Added
- Defined rows as students and columns as subjects
- Added comments for clarity of data structure

Changed
- Improved formatting of dataset for better readability

---

[v1.2] – 2025-09-12
Added
- Implemented functionality to access a specific score using indexing
- Tested retrieval of values from the 2D array

---

[v1.3] – 2025-10-03
Added
- Implemented score update functionality

Changed
- Improved handling of data modification within the array

---

[v1.4] – 2025-10-21
Added
- Implemented average calculation for student scores
- Displayed computed averages

Changed
- Improved output formatting for readability

---

[v1.4.1] – 2025-11-10 (Minor Patch)
Fixed
- Minor issues in average calculation formatting
- Improved variable naming for clarity

---

[v1.5] – 2025-11-26
Final (Python Version)
- Final review of dataset logic and structure
- Cleaned up comments and formatting
- Prepared initial version for submission

---

[v2.0] – 2026-02-16
Major Update (Web App Transition)

Added
- Converted project into a web-based application (HTML, CSS, JavaScript)
- Created interactive user interface for inputting and displaying scores
- Added dynamic table rendering using DOM manipulation
- Implemented real-time score updates and retrieval

Changed
- Migrated from Python implementation to JavaScript 2D arrays
- Improved usability and accessibility
- Prepared project for GitHub Pages deployment

---

[v2.1] – 2026-03-01
Added
- Introduced application branding: ScoreTrackr
- Added average column for performance overview
- Improved UI design (layout, colors, buttons)

Changed
- Enhanced user experience
- Improved input validation

---

[v2.2] – 2026-04-XX
Major System Refinement (Final Version)

Added
- Renamed system to GradeTrackr
- Added support for dynamic subjects and students
- Implemented remove functionality for subjects and students
- Added Upgrade Grade feature
- Added Get Grade feature using user-friendly indexing
- Implemented grade validation (0–99, max 2 digits)
- Added numbered indexing display for subjects and students
- Added section separators for better UI structure

Changed
- Replaced "score" terminology with "grade"
- Improved table structure (separate student number column)
- Updated subject labels format to [#] Subject Name
- Optimized data handling to maintain 2D array integrity

Fixed
- Resolved table misalignment when deleting rows/columns
- Fixed input overflow issues for grade values

---

Final Version
- Fully functional GradeTrackr system
- Stable data structure and UI
- Ready for academic submission
